I1. Project Objectives
The objectives of this project are:
Present updatesfor Transfer Station Update Phase 2 and Phase3Design options for
the City's consideration.
Prepare a full design of the City's selected options to Transfer Station Update Phase2
and Phase 3 Design.
Prepare Construction Bidding documentas required by City of Cheyenne's
purchasing department which includes thebidding document for Phase2Transfer
Station Update”and aseparate Construction Bidding document for Phase3"Transfer
Station Expansion."
Perform Construction Administration for Phase 2“Transfer Station Update”and a
separate Construction Administration for Phase3"Transfer Station Expansion”on an
hourlyrate.Mileage and drive time to location may notbe added to thecost of the
Construction Administration hourly rate.
III.Scope of Services
The minimum scope of services related to this project includes the following: The Consultant is
invited to provide additional steps or work tasks as they see fit to assist in the completion of the
objective.
A.
The consultant shall meet with City staff to gain an understanding of the work already
completed on the project.
B.
Update Phase2and Phase3Design.
C.
The consultant shall prepare an Operations Manual to ensure optimal operations of the
facility.Suggested comments and additions should be provided by the Consultant to
enhance the City's ability to operate thefacility in an efficient and safe manner.
D.
The consultant and City Staff shall expect to meet frequently, atleast bi-monthly, with
City staff during the designphase and on a weeklybasis during the Construction
Administration phase.
E.
The consultant shall research and make accommodation for two City of Cheyenne
representatives to a tour two separate facilities of similar size andvolume of MsW(150-
200 tons/day) as the City's Transfer Station. Both facilities must be located in the
continental United States.
IV.Materials/Information to be Provided by the Cityof Cheyenne
The following documents will be provided to the consultant by the City of Cheyenne
Public Works Office:
