V.
General Criteria for Evaluating Qualification Statements.
Experience:
The experience of the proposed consultants should be documented, particularly experience in
projects similar to the project proposed by the City of Cheyenne.Consultant experience will
be evaluated on the basis of consulting firms that have designed similar typesof facilities in
the solid waste industry for the transport and disposal of municipal solid waste (MsW).
Expertise:
Specific expertise is desirable ina variety ofareas including the following:
Developing designcost estimates that are within five percent of actual costs.
Professional references shall beprovided as practicable.
Working knowledge of the WD EQ rules for collection and transfer of MS W.
Workability:
The qualification statement should provide assurance of the ability of the consultant towork
witha diverse group of individuals and agencies including elected officials, citizens, property
owners, businesses, and governmental organizations.
Conflictsof Interest:
The qualification statement shall specifically address any possible conflicts of interest and
the proposer'sposition orresponse asto whether or not suchother work or relationship may
be deemed a conflict of interest with this project.
Special Qualifications:
The qualification statement shall identify any specific qualifications which might make the
proposer uniquely qualified to provide the requested services.These mayinclude similar
work experience related to another community of similar size or a project of similar design.
Professional Staff:
The experience ofthe proposed consultant's personnel assigned to this project shallbe noted.
Individual biographical resumes with specific project experience related to the work task
outlined in this request for proposals shall beincluded.
